00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:07.430 align:start position:0%
eu finance and economy ministers will  discuss better ways to help improve  access to funding for small and  medium-sized enterprises in talks in  luxembourg on october 15.  fallout from the crisis and general  economic ill health have created deep  uncertainty in the financial sector with  smes undergrowing financial pressure the  ministers will look at potential risk  sharing instruments like a joint  guarantee scheme for new loans which  would be partly financed with eu money  the decisions are part of preparations  for a meeting of eu heads of state and  government in brussels on the 24th and  25th of october  they'll also pave the way for talks  between the leaders on possible areas  for strengthening economic policy  coordination  also on the agenda in luxembourg is an  exchange of views on the lessons learned  from the european semester process  this helps eu member states to better  monitor their budgets and economic  policies  the aim of the talks is to draw  conclusions from the process in 2013  which ended on july 9 when  country-specific recommendations were  adopted and planned the way ahead for  the next year  the next european semester cycle gets  underway in november when the commission  will publish its annual growth survey  its view of the eu's policy priorities  for 2014.
 

